{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792360946,"nonce":"GvFZ4ez4Tjna6b7sjw2Jyr5LbTk=","message":"**The freeze after paging through the nav bar**\n\nCause: each visit to Navigate built the street map's path meshes (tens of MB per visit) and the Ash collector did not give them back, so after about ten laps the 512 MiB heap was full and the page spent its time collecting while the audio agent played on. The other pages stay flat. The collector side is with Ash (gc-verify shows a ScenePainter/CanvasPainter holder whose allocation record is 80 bytes against a 168/128-byte class); the allocation-log results were sent to ash-7d.\n\nIn the app (aa0105a, 79e0b2d): the map card is built once and parked off-screen while another page shows, with the new Canvas retain so its painter keeps its buffers. Navigate/More for 14 laps stays at about 127 MB (it thrashed at lap 7 before); a 160-click random run with music, orbit and sweeps ends at 154-182 MB with no failures.\n\nTest: dashboard_check.mjs now goes through every page eight times, turning the car between, and requires the page to still draw and the live heap to stay under 300 MB.\n\nReproducer for Ash: git checkout 2fe21bf -- apps/dashboard/src/dashboard/Dashboard.hx apps/dashboard/src/dashboard/NavigateView.hx haxe/ashui/ui/Canvas.hx haxe/ashui/core/render/CanvasPainter.hx, build the dashboard for the web, open it with ?env=ASH_GC_STATS=1 and click Navigate, More alternately.","files":null}]}